%S A400375 0,11,22,33,44,55,66,77,88,99,101,110,123,134,145,156,167,178,189,202,
%T A400375 211,220,235,246,257,268,279,303,312,321,330,347,358,369,404,413,422,
%U A400375 431,440,459,505,514,523,532,541,550,606,615,624,633,642,651,660,707,716
%N A400375 Numbers whose greedy alternating digit sum is 0 (in base 10).
%C A400375 The greedy alternating digit sum starts with S = 0. Then, for each successive decimal digit d, if S - d >= 0, subtract the digit from S, otherwise add.
%H A400375 Michael S. Branicky, <a href="/A400375/b400375.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%e A400375 2211 is a term since 0 + 2 = 2, 2 - 2 = 0, 0 + 1 = 1 and 1 - 1 = 0.
%o A400375 (Python)
%o A400375 def ok(n):
%o A400375     digits, S = list(map(int, str(n))), 0
%o A400375     [(S:=S-d if S-d >= 0 else S+d) for d in digits]
%o A400375     return S == 0
%o A400375 print([k for k in range(720) if ok(k)]) # _Michael S. Branicky_, Sep 27 2026
%K A400375 nonn,base,new
%O A400375 1,2
%A A400375 _Yaroslav Deryavko_, Sep 24 2026
